fix(touch): arm the GENI TX watermark and abort commands that stop moving

Comparing kt_i2c_write() with Qualcomm's i2c-qcom-geni.c FIFO path found
three differences, all in the first real transaction this driver ever got
to issue:

  - the FIFO write path never armed SE_GENI_TX_WATERMARK_REG.  Linux writes
    1 to it right after the command word ("Get FIFO IRQ"), and that is what
    makes the watermark status bit rise; this driver waited for a bit that
    could not arrive and timed out with M_IRQ_STATUS 0;
  - the NACK bit was tested as bit 9, but M_GP_IRQ_1_EN is bit 10 (bit 9 is
    GP_IRQ_0), so a real NACK would have been reported as an unknown error;
  - a timed-out command was only printed and left active.  Add kt_se_abort(),
    which writes M_CMD_ABORT_EN to SE_GENI_M_CMD_CTRL_REG, polls the abort
    status with the same bounded loop, then clears the IRQ status and the TX
    watermark, mirroring geni_cancel_m_cmd()/geni_abort_m_cmd().

The read-only probe also prints TX_WATERMARK and M_IRQ_EN now, so the next
run can show the handshake state instead of inferring it.

No transfer is sent from the boot path; this only changes what TOUCHINIT
does when it is asked to run.

--- a/bsd/dev/kebab_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/kebab_touch.c
@@ -254,7 +254,8 @@
 #define M_CMD_FAILURE           (1u << 3)
 #define M_CMD_CANCEL            (1u << 4)
 #define M_CMD_ABORT             (1u << 5)
-#define M_GP_IRQ_1_NACK         (1u << 9)
+#define M_GP_IRQ_0              (1u << 9)
+#define M_GP_IRQ_1_NACK         (1u << 10)
 #define M_RX_FIFO_WATERMARK     (1u << 26)
 #define M_RX_FIFO_LAST          (1u << 27)
 #define M_TX_FIFO_WATERMARK     (1u << 30)
@@ -1152,6 +1153,8 @@
